NAME
    
	fft - Fast Fourier Transform
    
SYNOPSIS
    
	vector<F> fft(vector<F> P);

PARAMETERS

	P    -    input polynomial of size N, a power of 2

RETURN VALUE

	returns a list of P(w^k) where 0 <= k < N, where w is any N-th root of unity.

REQUIREMENT

	F should be a field where N-th root of unity exists. For finite field F, that means |F| - 1 is divisible by N.

NOTES

	The choice of the root of unity w is deterministic, which only depends on the field F and size N.

COMPLEXITY

	O(N log N).

IMPLEMENTATION

	KACTL
